out={};text="# Next eight-player decision sheet — 2026-11-10\n\nSupersedes the eight-player shortlist disposition in [NEXT_RATING_BATCH_REVIEW.md](NEXT_RATING_BATCH_REVIEW.md); the20-player screen and remaining issue ledger stay open. Six offensive subparts are ready for the backend implementation queue. Herro handling and Paolo passing are held; Castle/Paolo defensive candidates await the shared correction. This is not a requirement to install eight player edits.\n\n## Frozen v11 context and ownership\n\nRead [v11 implementation report](../FIVE_PLAYER_CALIBRATION_IMPLEMENTATION_2026_11_10.md): all eleven earlier targets are installed for new careers; none is held. Its real card evidence and bounded game/trade tests belong to that report, not this research lane. The current [manifest](probe_artifacts/next_batch_refinement_manifest_20261110.json) freezes canonical version/hash plus eight consumer source hashes; the [compressed input](probe_artifacts/next_batch_refinement_input_20261110.json.gz) isolates analysis from concurrent changes. Initial canonical SHA-256 is "+hashlib.sha256(gzip.decompress((A/'next_batch_refinement_input_20261110.json.gz').read_bytes())).hexdigest()+". Code drift recorded after calculation means this is a pre-shared-fix diagnostic only.\n\nBackend owns shared formulas, implementation, market/game checks and tests. Research owns judgments and private fixed-context summaries here. No market rebuild, bidding round, negotiation simulation, game call, save or server action ran. The original eight combined calculations remain historical; separate subparts below reveal what can stand alone.\n\nOctober20,2026 is the cutoff. Inputs mix March skill rows, June subjective priors, preservation and later roster/career/profile updates. No uniform July label applies. Opening-week anecdotes are excluded. Identity confirmations remain resolved; the solid passer/defender wording near SF01:31:19 refers to Durant, not Kawhi. No rank target or promise/availability adjustment is used.\n\n## Subpart decisions\n\nAll shortlist traits are inferred, not direct observations. Observed inputs may include box rates, play-type usage or tracking proxies, but missing fields and opaque source windows remain. Versatility reflects play-type field breadth/usage; handle combines creation, turnover avoidance, PnR and touches; passing combines passer/assist/creation/IQ inputs; effort/navigation and rim traits use correlated event/role/size/impact proxies. June CSV values are subjective priors mapped through a cohort distribution. Proposed overlays are scouting decisions, not newly measured inputs. Current proposed traits below carry league calibration plus preserved-baseline markers; none already contains this proposed next-batch overlay.\n\nSG=[shooting guards](SHOOTING_GUARDS_TOP_10_FULL_EXTRACTION.md), SF=[small forwards](SMALL_FORWARDS_FULL_EXTRACTION.md), PF=[power forwards](POWER_FORWARD_FULL_EXTRACTION.md), PG=[point guards](POINT_GUARDS_FULL_EXTRACTION.md). Publication dates: SG Aug14, SF Aug19, PF Aug28, PG Aug5,2026. Speakers remain unidentified turns; opposing judgments are retained. Exact decisive text is in the [cue-check artifact](probe_artifacts/next_batch_decisive_cues_20261110.txt).\n\n| Subpart / stable player | Decision and candidate | Exact retained evidence: strengths / counterevidence | Magnitude and independence | Intended behavior |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n"
